{
  "capture": "telemetry/mg90-d__dev-v006-2A-D/load",
  "notes": "stage 3 load of mg90-d on dev-v006-2A-D, sitting servo-load-1 (the rig on its side, the printed arm on the horn, 22 US quarters in the outer cup pair, 5 V; blocks bottom-1, ladder-1, lift-1, steps-1; push not run). Torques absolute: gravity's torque at horizontal is the coins at the mint spec (5.670 g each, not weighed alone, +/-1 %) at the outer pair's CAD radius plus the arm weighed by hand on a kitchen scale (whole arm 166 g, block with lid, quarters and screws 153 g): block + lid + screws at the cups' center, the load mount at its STL centroid; gravity_torque_scale is that over the coins alone, bounds the coins' 1 % and 1 g moved between block and mount. Angles through the pot-table table, linear past its ends at the end rows' slope, from bottom_counts, the 12 % rests' degree midpoint (bounds the plan's count midpoint and the hand reading). Currents over each sweep's torque-off zero, the stage 1 in-drive offset out; construction C (resistance result) for i_w and v_c. kt_gear: gravity's torque on i_w over the from-below rungs that moved, settled and stayed inside the soft limits; bounds span the three bottoms and the fit's se about each. friction_band_lower and hold_deadband_* are lower bounds: the from-above step of 6 % and the +/-5 % steps moved nothing. Stall lines over every settled rung of 6 % or more with a valid window, the three stop rungs included; the cubic v_c = V0 + R0 i + c i^3. Lift speeds the pot's slope over +/-12.5 ms, means over +/-2 deg windows past 30 ms; the loss share R_C (i_w - i_free) / Ke, both currents under construction C (the free 5 V ladder rung's own sweeps, the held duty's last window), over the free rung's speed less the loaded speed at 20 and 30 deg. Falls from 2 rows after the bridge opens; release friction gravity less J alpha from a quadratic over 80 ms, gravity the coins and the arm, J the coins, the block and lid and the mount as point masses and the reflected rotor and train (the beam's own spread left out); friction at the speed peak gravity at the peak of a 40 ms Savitzky-Golay speed; Coulomb and viscous by least squares over |w| > 20 deg/s with the same gravity and J. Steps: jump 1 to 3 ms after the flip, settled the last 50 ms, per % of the duty change; k6 and k7's step edges have no rows before the flip and are left out. One sitting, one servo.",
